 "definitions": {
  "frame": "all geometry in the MuJoCo world frame at one recorded qpos (C1a_ep3_s31 control t 224); URDF FK frame == MuJoCo world (link origin offset 0.09 mm, rot 0.0004 deg, align.json)",
  "pairing": "URDF link -> MJCF body by nearest sphere-centre-to-mesh-vertex (align.json): ee_finger_l1 -> MJCF ee_finger_l2, ee_finger_l2 -> MJCF ee_finger_l1 (swap confirmed by position)",
  "mjcf_surface": "area-uniform samples (1 per 0.5 mm^2) on the convex hull of every collision mesh geom of the body (MuJoCo collides meshes as convex hulls); samples buried >0.2 mm in another piece of the same body dropped; samples within 0.5 mm of a rigidly attached neighbour body's hull (palm top under link_*_arm_6 / FT sensor) dropped",
  "gap": "min_i |p - c_i| - r_i ; >0 = outside the sphere union. frac_out = fraction of samples with gap>0; out_* = statistics over outside samples only",
  "openings": "finger qpos = open value x {1, 0.5, 0} (open: r1/l1 -0.05, r2/l2 +0.05)",
  "source_capsules": "the capsules the server spheres are generated from (mujoco_source.gap_filling_capsules = bounding capsules fitted to MJCF mesh vertices; fingers: the same before --finger-cover) at radius scale 1.0. The URDF file itself has 0 collision capsules on the 6 hand links",
  "excess": "1 mm voxels inside the link's own sphere union and outside every collision hull of that body; protrusion = max distance of such voxels to the hull surface samples",
  "contact_points": "recorded control-row qpos t_first..t_last+1 (replay qpos_mismatch_rows 0); for each (hand geom, fruit geom) pair of the event: mj_geomDistance <=1 mm (fromto hand point) or, when penetrating, the MuJoCo contact.pos of that pair",
  "channel": "palm frame along the tip direction (palm origin -> finger mid, perpendicular to the finger axis u): tip-most extent of palm spheres with |u.(c-mid)| < finger inner half gap + r, vs palm mesh samples in the same channel",
  "candidates": "offline only, nothing implemented: palm_scale1 = capsule_radius_scale_by_link {ee_left:1, ee_right:1}; palm_body_oX = gripper_cover.finger_body_spheres applied to the palm link_surface (spacing 1 mm, candidate grid 2 mm, union_eps 1 mm; not the finger defaults 0.5/0.5 mm), overflow X mm, replacing the palm gap-filling capsules"
